      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Lambda Anatomy and Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Lambda Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lambda = ==syntactic sugar== for an **unnamed closure class**",
                "The class has an `operator()`, ==const by default==",
                "One lambda expression creates ==one closure object=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Syntax",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`[captures](params) specifiers -> ret { body }`",
                "Return type is **deduced** from the body",
                "`-> ret` needed when {red:return statements disagree} or deduction gives the wrong type"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "auto add = [](int a, int b){ return a + b; };",
                "add(2, 3);  // 5",
                "auto f = [](bool b) -> double {",
                "    if (b) return 1;  // int vs double",
                "    return 2.5;",
                "};"
              ],
              "note": "-> double resolves the int/double clash"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Closure Type",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Case",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Two identical-looking lambdas",
                  "{red:different} closure types"
                ],
                [
                  "Captureless lambda to function pointer",
                  "{green:implicit} conversion"
                ],
                [
                  "Capturing lambda to function pointer",
                  "{red:not allowed}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Each lambda expression has its ==own unique type==. Never name it; use `auto`, a template, or `decltype`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Captures: Value, Reference, Mutable",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Captures: Value, Reference, Mutable",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Value vs Reference",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Capture",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`[x]`",
                  "==copy== made at creation; later changes not seen"
                ],
                [
                  "`[&x]`",
                  "reference to the ==original=="
                ],
                [
                  "`[=]` / `[&]`",
                  "all used locals by value / by reference"
                ],
                [
                  "`[=, &y]`",
                  "all by value, y by reference"
                ],
                [
                  "`[&, x]`",
                  "all by reference, x by value"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Mutable and Init-Capture",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "By-value copy is ==const== inside `operator()`",
                "Add `mutable` to modify the copy",
                "The original stays {green:unchanged}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "int n = 0;",
                "auto f = [n]() mutable { return ++n; };",
                "f(); f();  // 1, then 2; outer n is still 0"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Init-capture== (C++14) names a new member",
                "Enables {purple:move-only} and computed captures"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "auto g = [p = std::move(ptr), v = x*2]{ };"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Capturing this",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`[this]` copies the ==pointer==, not the object",
                "`[*this]` (C++17) copies the ==whole object==",
                "C++20 deprecates implicit this via `[=]` (warns); write `[=, this]` or `[=, *this]`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pointer risk",
              "text": "`[this]` dangles if the object dies first; `[*this]` is safe."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Generic Lambdas and Function Objects",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Generic Lambdas and Function Objects",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Generic lambdas",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`auto` params (C++14) make ==operator()== a template",
                "Works with int, double, std::string",
                "C++20 `[]<typename T>` names ==T== and constrains the shape"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "auto add = [](auto a, auto b){ return a + b; };",
                "add(1, 2); add(1.5, 2.5); add(s1, s2);",
                "auto n = []<typename T>(std::vector<T>& v){",
                "    return v.size();",
                "};"
              ],
              "note": "one lambda, many types"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Function objects",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Functor = a ==named type== with `operator()`, can hold **state**",
                "`std::plus<>`, `std::greater<>`, `std::less<>` are standard functors",
                "Transparent `<>` form ==deduces== the types"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "struct Add {",
                "    int operator()(int a, int b) const { return a+b; }",
                "};",
                "std::sort(v.begin(), v.end(), std::greater<>{});"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Lambda vs functor",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Lambda",
                "Functor"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Size",
                  "**Short**, local",
                  "Longer"
                ],
                [
                  "Type",
                  "Unnamed",
                  "**Named**, reusable"
                ],
                [
                  "Overloads",
                  "One `operator()`",
                  "Many"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Choose",
              "text": "Use a ==named functor== when the type is needed in several places or has multiple overloads."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "std::function vs Templates",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "std::function vs Templates",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Template Parameter",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`template<class F> void run(F f)` keeps the ==exact closure type==",
                "Call is {green:inlinable} with **no allocation**: the fastest option"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "template<class F>",
                "void run(F f) { f(); }",
                "",
                "run([&]{ work(); });"
              ],
              "note": "each lambda instantiates its own run"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. std::function",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`std::function<R(Args...)>` ==type-erases== any callable",
                "Storable in members and containers; reassignable at runtime",
                "Cost: {red:indirect call}, maybe a **heap allocation** for big captures"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Needs a ==copyable== callable: a move-only lambda fails",
                "Use `std::move_only_function` (C++23) or a template"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Choosing One",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Called immediately",
                  "template `F`"
                ],
                [
                  "Stored or runtime-swapped",
                  "`std::function`"
                ],
                [
                  "Cheap non-owning param",
                  "`std::function_ref` (C++26) or function pointer"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::vector<std::function<void()>> tasks;",
                "tasks.push_back([&]{ work(); });",
                "tasks.push_back([]{ log(); });"
              ],
              "note": "different lambdas, one container"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Default",
              "text": "Start with a **template**. Reach for ==std::function== only when you must store or swap the callable."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dangling Captures and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Dangling Captures and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Dangling References",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Returned or stored `[&]` lambda outlives its locals: {red:dangling refs} = ==undefined behavior==",
                "Same trap: threads, async tasks, stored callbacks",
                "Fix: capture ==by value== or init-capture",
                "Never let a reference-capturing lambda outlive its scope"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "auto bad() { int x = 1; return [&]{ return x; }; }  // UB",
                "auto ok()  { int x = 1; return [x]{ return x; }; }",
                "auto ok2() { int x = 1; return [v = x]{ return v; }; }"
              ],
              "note": "x dies when bad() returns"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dangling this and Lost State",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`[this]` callback outlives object: dangling pointer",
                  "`[*this]` (copy) or `[self = shared_from_this()]`"
                ],
                [
                  "Mutable by-value lambda copied into `std::function` or algorithm: works on the copy, state lost",
                  "`[&]` or `std::ref` for shared state"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Default Captures",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`[=]` and `[&]` hide what is captured",
                "Stored or async lambda: ==list captures explicitly=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Escapes scope?",
              "text": "Capture by ==value==, never `[&]`. `[this]` is a pointer, so it is only as safe as the object."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
