          "title": "Lambda Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Syntax and Captures",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "[capture](params) mutable constexpr noexcept -> ret { body }",
                "auto f = [] {};  // [] and {} are the only mandatory parts"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Capture",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`[x]`",
                  "copy of x"
                ],
                [
                  "`[&x]`",
                  "reference to x"
                ],
                [
                  "`[=]`",
                  "all used, by copy"
                ],
                [
                  "`[&]`",
                  "all used, by reference"
                ],
                [
                  "`[x=expr]`",
                  "init-capture"
                ],
                [
                  "`[this]`",
                  "pointer only"
                ],
                [
                  "`[*this]`",
                  "copy of the object"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Choose a Callable Type",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Called inside the function",
                  "template `F`"
                ],
                [
                  "Stored or swappable",
                  "`std::function`"
                ],
                [
                  "Captureless C API",
                  "function pointer"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Safe Rules",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Escapes the scope: capture ==by value==",
                "By reference only for immediate use: `std::sort`, `for_each`",
                "Move-only: init-capture `[p = std::move(up)]`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why is operator() const?** Captured copies are read-only; ==mutable== lets them change",
                "**Template over std::function?** Called immediately: inlinable, no allocation",
                "**[&] in a returned lambda?** ==Dangling references==, undefined behavior",
                "**Capture a unique_ptr?** Init-capture with `std::move`; the lambda becomes move-only"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
