              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What does this print?",
              "example_code": [
                "int n = 0;",
                "auto f = [n]() mutable { return ++n; };",
                "f(); f();",
                "std::cout << f() << n;"
              ],
              "a_bullets": [
                "`30`",
                "The closure holds its own copy of n, so f() returns 3 and the outer n stays 0."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Spot the bug: `auto make(){ int x=1; return [&]{ return x; }; }`",
              "a_bullets": [
                "x dies when make returns, so the lambda holds a dangling reference (UB).",
                "Fix: capture by value, `[x]{ return x; }`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Why does `std::function<void()> g = [p = std::make_unique<int>(1)]{};` not compile?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "std::function needs a copyable callable, and a closure holding a unique_ptr is move-only.",
                "Use a template parameter or `std::move_only_function` (C++23)."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
